{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/pulls/8730","id":4631248190,"node_id":"PR_kwDOMMa-Ps8AAAABFAs9Pg","html_url":"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-ai/pull/8730","diff_url":"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-ai/pull/8730.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-ai/pull/8730.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/issues/8730","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/pulls/8730/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/pulls/8730/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/issues/8730/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/statuses/76f731a2aa15b82abbe5c0d3397fb0bc9b9f11d0","number":8730,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Keep the type variable of a generic `OutputSpec[T]` passed to `Agent.run` under mypy","user":{"login":"DouweM","id":159434,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1OTQzNA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/159434?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DouweM","html_url":"https://github.com/DouweM","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DouweM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DouweM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DouweM/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DouweM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DouweM/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DouweM/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DouweM/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DouweM/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DouweM/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Since 2.49.0, mypy infers `AgentRunResult[Any]` when a generic `OutputSpec[T]` is passed on to `run`, `run_sync`, `run_stream` or `iter`, which fires `no-any-return` under `--strict`. #8641 put the private `_NoneOutput` protocol (which lets `[Foo, None]` type as `Foo | None`) inside the recursive `Sequence` element of `OutputSpec`, and mypy can't solve the type variable through it. This gives a list with a bare `None` its own branch, one level deep, and leaves the recursive `Sequence['OutputSpec[T_co]']` as it was before #8641.\n\nThanks @jukebox for the precise report and for pointing at the exact line.\n\n- Closes #8717\n\nWhat each checker infers, before (main) → after:\n\n| Case | mypy 2.1.0 | pyright 1.1.414 | pyright 1.1.411 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `agent.run(..., output_type=spec)` with `spec: OutputSpec[T]` (also `run_sync`, `run_stream`, `iter`) | `AgentRunResult[Any]` → `AgentRunResult[T]` | `AgentRunResult[T]`, unchanged | `AgentRunResult[T]`, unchanged |\n| `[Foo, Bar, None]`, `[ToolOutput(Foo), None]`, `[[Foo, None], Bar]` | unchanged (mypy doesn't infer list outputs either way) | `... \\| None`, unchanged | `... \\| None`, unchanged |\n| `NativeOutput([Foo, None])`, `ToolOutput(None, ...)` | unchanged | unchanged | unchanged |\n| `Annotated[float, ...]`, `Literal['a', 'b']`, `Foo \\| Bar` | unchanged (refused, as documented) | unchanged (`TypeForm`) | unchanged |\n\n`tests/typed_agent.py` (checked by `make typecheck-mypy` in CI) now pins generic forwarding through all four run methods; on main those pins fail mypy with 6 errors. pyright 1.1.411 reports the same set of errors on `tests/typed_agent.py` and `tests/typed_output.py` before and after this change.\n\nAlternatives I tried:\n- Dropping `_NoneOutput` from the alias entirely also fixes mypy, and pyright 1.1.412+ still accepts `None` as a `TypeForm`, but `[Foo, None]` stops type-checking on pyright 1.1.411.\n- Moving `_NoneOutput` into `_OutputSpecItem` also fixes mypy, but it makes a bare `output_type=None` type-check on older pyright, even though that raises at run time.\n- `TypeForm` (#8690) is not involved: with `_NoneOutput` out of the recursion, mypy solves `T` with `TypeForm` in `OutputTypeOrFunction`.\n\nTrade-off: on pyright before 1.1.412, a list with both a nested list and a bare `None` at the same level (`[Foo, [Bar, None], None]`) no longer type-checks. It did for the two days since #8641 shipped. Pyright 1.1.412 and later still accept it as a `TypeForm`, and mypy never did. Fixing the regression for mypy users seemed more important than that edge case on older pyright.\n\n### Checklist\n\n- [ ] Any **AI generated code** has been reviewed line-by-line by the human PR author, who stands by it.\n- [x] No **breaking changes** in accordance with the [version policy](https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-ai/blob/main/docs/version-policy.md).\n- [x] Any permitted **compatibility impact** has a label, warning, migration, release note, and exact API-check waiver.\n- [x] **PR title** is fit for the [release changelog](https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-ai/releases).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/pydantic/pydantic-ai/pull/8730?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n","labels":[{"id":7110547176,"node_id":"LA_kwDOMMa-Ps8AAAABp9JW6A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"Report that something isn't working, or PR implementing a fix","color":"d73a4a","default":true,"archived_at"